      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just to clarify: it might seem like a meaningless thing, because it's not causing the avatar to jitter, but it becomes a problem when you need to have a PhysBone on an object that is outside the humanoid rig. \n\nThe PhysBones that are not part of the humanoid rig jitter with the root, no matter if their parent object is constrained to the humanoid rig, uses a rigid body joint or IK - the root jiter always propagates to them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
